1 NOTE HIs parents moved from Lebanon, ME to Oshkosh, WI.  They later moved to Nekimi, WI in 1849.  and still later to concord, Dodge co., MN
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary printed in teh West Concord newspaper:
2 CONT "In 1851, William Chadbourne Tibbetts and his wife removed to Concord Towship, Didge Co., MN, which ha ever since been his home.  For many years they lived on thier farm half a mile west of Concord, but in 1895, they moved into th
2 CONC e village where they lived until after the death of his wife a little more than a year ago.  He then moved into West Concord to be with his only surviving child, Adelbert.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Tibbetts has been an active, conscientious Christian for the last forty years, having taken part in the work before uniting with the Baptist Church on FE. 1, 1870.  Later he and his wife placed their membership with the Church
2 CONC  of Christ near their home and remained members of that church until death.  He was Superintendant of the Sunday School for many years and often conducted the church services in the absence of the pastor.  He had a conservative na
2 CONC ture but was one to whom many went for advice and on whose judgmnet much relaince was placed."
1 CHAN
2 DATE 17 JUL 2023
3 TIME 06:02:50
