1 NOTE
2 CONT January 16, 1917 - Peter A. Holje died at his home in the town of Black Hammer at 4:30 p.m. January 8, 1917.  Peter Holje was born in Toten, Norway, September 9, 1859.  He came with his parents to America in 1869, coming direct to
2 CONC  Spring Grove.  In 1904 he bought a small farm in Black Hammer where he has made his home since.  Mr. Holje was married May 31, 1890 to Miss Ingeborg B. Veum.  They have no children.  His wife died November 6, 1916, a little over 
2 CONC two months ago. Funeral services were held on Thursday January 11th, his body laid to rest beside that of his wife in the Black Hammer Cemetery.  Rev. Frost officiated.  Mr. Holje has been aiing for the past 20 years.
2 CONT He leaves four brothers and four sisters:  Helmer Holje and Mrs. Olaf Gran of Spring Grove; Paul Hanon of Elbow Lake, MN; Carl of Esmond, ND; Peder of Flora, ND; Mrs. Hans Hauge of Coarissa, MN; Mrs. J. Bangsberg of La Crosse and 
2 CONC Mrs. Peter Narum of Dodge Center, MN.
