2 CONT
2 CONT [Letter to Hilda, Daughter of Peter Anton Grahn of Australia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Buckley Wash May 1, 1921
2 CONT
2 CONT Dear Hilda,
2 CONT      Well, Well, after some 30 years again I hear from Peter's family in Australia.  To my sorrow I learn there are only 3 left of my brother's family, also, because only girls are left his name will not sound more in Australia.  
2 CONC Same with me, had only 2 girls Ellen & Olga.  Nothing to do with it.  I and my wife are getting old.  I am 67 & she 66 and thus we are nearing the end.  Well, this is the way of the world.  Man like everything else are born for to
2 CONC  grow, reproduce & die, and it would not be well if it was not so.
2 CONT      So I will tell about my family.  Ellen my oldest girl died about 9 years ago.  She married into the President Cleveland family.  Her husband name was Harry Cleveland from New York City.  They had one son and his name is Rober
2 CONC t Gran Cleveland and if you like to write him address 11-West 11th ST. New York City c/o Mrs. Mead who is sister of his father.  He is now 11 years old and a good writer.  His handwriting is like your father's.  He will answer you
2 CONC .  He has been with his sister since Ellen died.  Our youngest daughter Olga lives in Seattle.  She is married & her husband's name is E. F. Wheeler and their address is 5035 7th ave N.E.  Seattle Wash.  They have 2 girls, Catheri
2 CONC ne 6 years and Dorothea 10 months.  Once in a while we are down visiting them & Catherine will come & stay with us part of the summer.  You also have other relatives in Seattle, that is the children of brother Peder Gran.  His old
2 CONC est son Henry is an automobile merchant there.  He was the first one selling automobiles in Seattle and is well to do.  His address Henry Grant (he calls himself Grant instead of Gran) Seattle Automobile Co., Seattle, Wash.  So yo
2 CONC u have the oldest daughter of sister Jorgine.  Her address Mrs. Ole Mol, Chula Vista, California.  She has other brothers and sisters, most of them living in Minnesota but don't know their addresses.  So you have the relations of 
2 CONC sister Juliane.  She has a daughter of Kenosha, Wisconsin and all I know is that her married name is Mrs. Sorensen.  Juliane has a son at Bella Coola, B.C. Canada.  He calls himself Hans Odegaard.  Of Paul Grans children are now o
2 CONC nly 2 left, that is myself & my oldest sister Juliane in Norway.  She is now about 90 years old.  I was over in Norway in 1914.  Then she was about 82 but still a good walker and nothing the matter with her.
2 CONT      You call me Lumber Merchant but I never was.  I withdrew from it & the firm never started.  I have been in General Merchandise most of the time & for about the last 10 years been dealing in shoes.  Now I have only my repairin
2 CONC g shop.
2 CONT      Weather & wind nothing to write about as you are living in the tropics & I in the temperate, finest climate in the world..., except the summer of Norway.  I was in Norway when Kaiser Wilhelm started this terrible world war wh
2 CONC ich is liable to end the Capitalist system before peace will be established on earth again.  I see you have plenty of starvation in New South Wales too, and we have plenty  of it here, tho there is an overflow of all things.
2 CONT
2 CONT [signed]
2 CONT M. Gran
2 CONT [Martin Gran]
2 CONT
