2 CONT  Buckley Banner (WA)  Friday 2_March1924
2 CONT Martin Gran Dies
2 CONT Old Pioneer Passes Away at His Home in Buckley
2 CONT Martin Gran, a resident of Buckley for the past thirty years or more, passed away at his home Wednesday noon.  For the past several months he has 
2 CONT >been in ill health, although he was able to be up and around.  The last few days, however, he had been confined to his home and Mrs. DuPue/DuPoe[?] had been engaged to take care of him.  Yesterday morning he took a walk and retur
2 CONC ned to the home looking somewhat fatigued and passed away a short time later, heart trouble being the cause.
2 CONT Mr. Gran was born July _[?2]4, 1854, in Norway but came to this country when a young boy,  ________________ ten years ____________________________________ he came to Buckley and engaged in ____________________________  ten years a
2 CONC go so retired from active life and took a trip to the old country returning here where he has lived ever since. 
2 CONT Mr. Gran was a good business man and at the time of his death owned several pieces of property in Buckley.  He was well thought of and had been invited as a guest to the banquet tonight given in honor of the pioneers of the town.
2 CONT Deceased had reached the age of ___ years, his wife died a year ago.  One daughter, Mrs. W. W[?] Wheeler of ______, a sister in Norway and a grandson in New York are left to mourn his death.
2 CONT Funeral services will be held in the Chapel of the Jones Undertaking Parlor here this afternoon at 2 o'clock.  Mr. Swain of  Enumclaw will be reading the service.  Interment will be in Buckley cemetery."
2 CONT
