1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Duane Marvin Samuelson of Kensington, died Tues, August 3, 2021 at Alomere Health, Alexandria. A Memorial Service was held Sat, August 7, 2021 at Messiah Lutheran Church, Hoffman, with Pastor Mark Mathews officiati
2 CONC ng. Burial at Solem Cemetery, Kensington.
2 CONT
2 CONT Duane was born to Morris and Lillian (Gunderson) Samuelson on July 4, 1952 at St. Lukes Hospital in Alexandria, MN. The building is still located a block west of Subway, south of the old Central Pool. He was baptized into the Chri
2 CONC stian Faith at Solem Lutheran Church, Kensington. While growing up in the Kensington area on the century farm where his mother was born and raised, he attended church, Sunday school, and was also confirmed at Solem Church. Duane a
2 CONC ttended and graduated from Hoffman High School where he was active in Band, Choir and FFA (Future Farmers of America). He was in 4-H where he was State Ambassador during the early years of the Minnesota Ambassador program. Duane f
2 CONC urthered his education at the University of MN, Crookston, graduating with a degree in agriculture. He went on to North Dakota State University, graduating with a degree in Agriculture Education.
2 CONT
2 CONT While attending a 4-H Citizenship Short Course in Washington, DC, Duane met Darlene Possehl. On June 29, 1974, Duane and Darlene were married at Trinity Lutheran Church in rural Sabin, MN. To this union, four children were born, A
2 CONC ndrew, Philip, Louis, and Jennifer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Duane worked in the loan department at United Federal Savings and Loan in Alexandria for ten years and was an instructor for thirty years at Alexandria Technical and Community College.
2 CONT
2 CONT Throughout his life, Duane was a member of Solem Lutheran in Kensington, Bethesda Lutheran in Alexandria, and Messiah Lutheran in Hoffman – being active on the church councils and choirs. He was on the Douglas County Extension Com
2 CONC mittee, was a 4-H adult leader, and was a member of the Douglas County Fair Board for 14 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Duane cherished his time spent with family, going on camping trips, fishing, and spending time outdoors working on his lawn, garden, and cutting wood.
2 CONT
2 CONT Duane is survived by his wife, Darlene of Kensington; 4 children, Andrew (Heather) Samuelson of Blaine, MN, Philip (Haley) Samuelson of Renner, SD, Louis Samuelson of Jamestown, ND, and Jennifer (Ty) Gangelhoff of Esko, MN; 7 gran
2 CONC dchildren, Logan, Brayden, Jack, Caleb, Julia, Callie and Elise; nieces, nephews, and a host of friends. He was preceded in death by his parents, Morris & Lillian, and sister, Mary Lou Smith.
2 CONT (obit: Erickson Smith Funeral Home)
