1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ole C. Nelson was born in Kensington, Minnesota, on August 27, 1893, the son of Christian and Julia (Sarsland) Nelson. He attended Kensington schools and also attended a business school for one year in Austin, Minn
2 CONC esota. On June 5, 1929, Ole was united in marriage to Mildred Samuelson of Barrett, Minnesota. They have celebrated their 57th wedding anniversary. Ole's lifetime occupation was farming and he farmed all his life at the same farm,
2 CONC  one mile north of Kensington. Mr. Nelson was a long time member of Solem Lutheran Church and served as Trustee. He was also a board member and treasurer of District 63 and board member of the Kensington Creamery.
2 CONT Ole died at the Douglas County Hospital on Monday, May 11, 1987. He is survived by his wife Mildred of Kensington; one daughter, Mrs. Marvin (Marlys) Jensen of Evansville, Minnesota; two sons, Omar Nelson of Taylor, Wisconsin, Ver
2 CONC nal Nelson of Kensington; eleven grandchildren and six great grandchildren. He was preceded in death by his parents, two sisters and six brothers.
2 CONT Funeral services were Thursday, May 14, 1987, 2:00 p.m. at Solem Lutheran Church with Reverend James Radatz officiating. Pallbearers were Paul Nelson, Joel Nelson, Keith Nelson, Dana Nelson, Mark Jensen and Jerry Briese. Interment
2 CONC  was at Solem Lutheran Cemetery, Kensington, Minnesota. Services were directed by Petermeier's Alexandria Funeral Home.
2 CONT (Lake Region Press, 22 May 1987)
