2 CONT Re: Bjerke's in Grant County 
2 CONT   Author: Tom Johnson  Date: 3 Jan 2002 5:35 AM GMT  
2 CONT   Classification: Query 
2 CONT   In Reply to: Bjerke's in Grant County  by:  Paul Steiner 
2 CONT Post Reply | Mark Unread | Report Abuse   Print Message  
2 CONT The book "History of Hoffman; 1891 - 1991" published for Hoffman Centennial, P. 83, has some info and a small family photo on Johannes and Anne Bjerke family. It says they homesteaded on land in Section 32 of Elk Lake Township. Th
2 CONC ey were early members of the Lincoln Congregation. Nine children were born to them: daughters Karen, Petra, Julia, Ellen, and Clara, and sons Even, Olof, John, and Freeman.
2 CONT In addition, on P. 84 there is a larger writeup of Even E. and Anna (Lee) Bjerke family. There are no entries on families of other kids. Found more info on Even and Anna Bjerke in "The Heritage of Grant County, Minnesota (1991)", 
2 CONC but again nothing on other kids. The Grant County Historical Society may have more info in their files and does research (within their files) for a nominal fee. Let me know if I can be of further assistance. Tom Johnson, Fergus Fa
2 CONC lls.
2 CONT
