1 NOTE Obituary:  May 3, 1936  Dehly-Agnes, of 1301 6th ave.. no., May f1, aged 82 beloved wife of Ferdinand Dehly; mother of Katie McConnell, Mrs.  Emilie Rhodes, Mrs. Amanda Johnson, Seattle, Mrs Anna Swain, Enumclaw, Wash.; Mrs. Flore
2 CONC nce Smith, Henry P., Adolph M., and Benjamin Grant.  Services Monday, 3 p.m.  Home undertaking Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT My Grandmother, Ardis Grant Steiner, told me the story that her Grandmother, Agnes had told her.  When she was a young girl living in a dirt house on the Plaines of Minnesota, the Indians invaded her family's home.  I'm not sure i
2 CONC f the family hid underneath the house, but apparently the only thing that the Indians took was a  hairbrush.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1900 US Census:
