2 CONT Gender: M 
2 CONT Date of Death: 04 Nov 1954 
2 CONT Certificate: 20104
2 CONT
2 CONT DEATH: Obit. The Washington Motorist
2 CONT Death Calls Henry P. Grant
2 CONT    It is with the utmost sorrow and regret that we report the death of Mr. H. P. Grant, charter member of the automobile Club of Washington, and only man ever the carry an AAA 50-Year membership card.
2 CONT    Mr. Grant passed away on November 4.  He had been ill for some time.
2 CONT    Mr. Grant earned the respect and admiration of the entire management and staff of the Automobile Club.  He often visited Club headquarters in Seattle, and these visits were always cheerful and happy events.  The association whi
2 CONC ch we have had with Mr. Grant have created treasured memories which we shall carry with us always.
2 CONT    Mr. Grant was to take part in the official ceremonies launching the Club's 50th Aniversary on November 10.  He was scheduled to sit in the place of honor at the head table at the Rotary meeting at which his part in early motor 
2 CONC club movement was to be lauded by AAA executive vice president, Russell E. Singer.
2 CONT    Mr. Grant was a member who set a perfect example of good driving.  Never in his entire life--fifty-one years of motoring--did Mr. Grant have a traffic accident.
2 CONT    Only a few men earn permanent niches in the records of history.  Mr. Grant was one of those men.
2 CONT    He shall be missed
