2 CONT Obituary: Seattle Times Feb. 23, 1951 p. B4
2 CONT MRS. CLARENCE K. MCCONELL RITES TOMORROW
2 CONT    Funeral services for Katherine G. McConnell, 78, of 767-1/2 Harrison St., who died Wednesday at her home after a brief illness, will be held at 3 o'clock tomorrow in the Green Lake chapel, followed by cremation.
2 CONT    Mrs. McConnell had lived here for 60 years.  She was born in Hoffman Minn.
2 CONT    She was a member of Our Redeemer's Lutheran Church.
2 CONT    She was the widow of Clarence K. McConnell.
2 CONT    Surviving are three sons, Walter M., Gerald A. and Ross S. McConnell, all of Seattle; a daughter, Mrs. Thelma Zimmerman, San Fransisco; two brothers, Henry P. and Adolph Grant, both of Seattle; four sisters, Mrs. Emily Rhodes, 
2 CONC Mrs. Amanda Phillips, and Mrs Anna Swain, all of Seattle, and Mrs. Florence Smith, Los Angeles; three grandchildren and two great-grandchildren.
