2 CONT Obituary: Seattle Times Tues., May 11, 1954
2 CONT MRS. BENNET SWAIN DIES AT HOME
2 CONT    Mrs. Anna M. Grant Swain, 71, widow of Bennet Swain former state representative died yesterday at her home after a sudden illness.
2 CONT    Mrs. Swain of 1717 E. John St. was a pioneer of Seattle. She came here a month before the fire of 1889, with her parents, the late Mr. and Mrs. Peter Grant.  Her father was a carpenter.
2 CONT    Mrs. Swain attended the old Denny School.  She moved to Enumclaw in 1916 and lived there until her husband's death five years ago when she returned to Seattle.  Her husband was in the Legislature in the 1920's.
2 CONT    Surviving are a son, Clifford Swain Port Angeles; two brothers, Henry P. Grant and Adolph Grant, both of Seattle; three sisters, Mrs. Amanda Phillips and Mrs Emily Rhodes, both of Seattle, and Mrs. Florence Smith, Los Angeles, 
2 CONC and two grandchildren.
2 CONT    Funeral services will be held at 2 o'clock Thursday in the Johnson & Hamilton chapel.  Cremation will follow.
