1 NOTE Buckley Banner (WA) Friday 20Apr1923
2 CONT >
2 CONT >"Last Wednesday at 11:00 a.m. at her home in Buckley Mrs. Carrie Gran passed 
2 CONT >to the next world, death being heart trouble.
2 CONT >
2 CONT >"The deceased was born in Norway, coming to this country in 1830[?], living 
2 CONT >at St. Paul, Minn. two years.  In 18__[?] she was united in marriage to 
2 CONT >Martin Gran and moved to Douglas County, Minnesota.  They moved to the state 
2 CONT >of Washington in 18__[?] and have resided in Buckley ever since.  Two 
2 CONT >children were born to this union, the eldest, Mrs. Miles Cleveland who died 
2 CONT >ten years ago and Mrs. Olga Wheeler, who resides in Seattle.  Besides her 
2 CONT >husband and daughter there are left to mourn three grandchildren, Robert 
2 CONT >from Cleveland, New York and Catherine and Dorothy Wheeler of Seattle, one 
2 CONT >brother, Mass[?] West___[?] of Norway, two sisters, Mrs. Chas. Newstrom of 
2 CONT >Tacoma and Mrs. G____ Nolan of Minneapolis.
2 CONT >
2 CONT >"At the time of her death Mrs. Gran had reached the age of 6_ years and __ 
2 CONT >days.
2 CONT >
2 CONT >"Mrs. Gran will be greatly missed among the people of Buckley as she was a 
2 CONT >kind hearted and loving woman, and the Banner joins with relatives and 
2 CONT >friends in extending condolences.
2 CONT >
2 CONT >"Funeral will be held this afternoon at 2 o'clock at the chapel.  Interment 
2 CONT >in Buckley cemetery."
2 CONT
2 CONT
