2 CONT WHEELER  OLGA    FEMALE  8 Feb 1889  25 Mar 1971  MINNESOTA  MARIN  547054209
2 CONT
2 CONT CENSUS: Wheeler, Olga  
2 CONT   Age: 39 Year: 1930 
2 CONT   Birthplace:   Roll:  T626_1953 
2 CONT   Race:   Page:  7A 
2 CONT   State: Oregon ED:  407 
2 CONT   County: Multnomah Image:  0219 
2 CONT   Township: Portland 
2 CONT   Relationship: Wife 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Independent Journal, Marin County, California, March 26, 1971
2 CONT
2 CONT OLGA WHEELER
2 CONT
2 CONT Olga Wheeler, a resident of 114 Del Casa Drive, Mill Valley, since 1955, died yesterday in a local hospital after a long illness.  She was 82.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born in Minnesota and came to California in 1930 with her husband, Elisha Wheeler, a frozen foods salesman.  After living briefly in Seattle and San Francisco, they moved to Mill Valley in 1955.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Wheeler was a member of the Chi Omega sorority at the University of Washington, Seattle, which she attended two years, and of the Episcopal Church of Our Savior, Mill Valley.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by her husband; two daughters, Catherine Lincoln and Dorothy W. Ortman, both of Mill Valley, and three grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Private service will be held tomorrow, with private butial to follow.  The family requests contributions to the Episcopal Church of Our Savior.
