1 NAME Lorraine /Holje/
2 GIVN Lorraine
2 SURN Holje
2 _MARNM Hvinden
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 PLAC North Viking Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Maddock
3 STAE North Dakota
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 7 JUN 1933
1 DEAT
2 DATE 20 DEC 1979
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/43292485/lorraine-hvinden
2 CONT
2 CONT Lorraine was born the daughter of Leonard and Mabel Bondeli Holje. She graduated from high school at BCATS in Maddock. Lorraine married Curtis Hvinden, the son of Herman and Cecelia Bergsgaard Hvinden. Together the couple raised f
2 CONC ive children, Steven, James, Sandra, Susan and Mark. She died at the Heart of America medical center of cancer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services for Mrs. Curtis (Lorraine) Hinden, 46, of rural Maddock were held on Sunday, 23 Dec 1979 at 2:00 p.m. in the Viking Lutheran Church. Interment was in the church cemetery. Rev's Dale Seffrood and Duane Neugebauer o
2 CONC fficiated.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Hvinden died on Thursday, 20 Dec 1979 in the Good Samaritan Hospital in Rugby following a lengthy illness.
2 CONT
2 CONT Casket bearers were Harlan Hellerud, Douglas Arnston, J. A. M. Shaffer, Merton Knatterud, Rolf Berg and Alton Liudahl. Mrs. Hvinden's friends in the community were designated as honorary pallbearers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lorraine Mabel Holje was born on 7 Jun 1933 the daughter of Leonard and Mabel Bondeli Holje near Maddock. She attended the Flora and Maddock schools and graduated from BCATS in 1950. She was united in marriage to Curtis Hvinden in
2 CONC  the North Viking Lutheran Church on 27 Oct 1951. The couple has farmed and resided southeast of Maddock since their marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lorraine was currently secretary of the Viking LCW; had been the first LCW president when the Viking LCW was merged; was a Sunday school teacher and an active 4-H leader.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are her husband; three sons, Steven of Fargo, James of Maddock and Mark at home; two daughters, Mrs. Jacob (Sandra) Hoffner of Maddock and Susan at home; her father, Leonard Holje of Maddock; two brothers, Marvin Holje o
2 CONC f Harvey and David Holje of Maddock and two grandchildren, Joshua Hoffner and Eric Hvinden.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her mother who died on 16 Mar 1979.
