1 OCCU Policeman
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Burial record and obituary:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/164188648/louis-solberg
2 CONT
2 CONT SOLBERG-Louis Solberg died Sunday. He was born June 6, 1835, in Christiana, Norway, and came to the United States in 1868, settling in Minneapolis in 1869. He married Mattie Lysue [sic] in 1874, who survives him, as do also three 
2 CONC children, Mrs. Frank L. Wenger, Milton Solberg and Alvilda Solberg. The funeral will be held from the family residence, 1204 Stevens avenue, at 2:30 o'clock this afternoon.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Minneapolis Tribune, August 27, 1907 page 5
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~
2 CONT
2 CONT An article in The Minneapolis Journal, August 24, 1907, states that “He was appointed to the police force by Eugene M. Wilson, the first mayor elected after the union of the cities. He served on the force for fifteen years and ret
2 CONC ired with an excellent record both for ability and honesty. He was active in cleaning the city of the early-day crooks and straightened out many beats that could not be handled by the other policemen.”
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis and Mattie married on December 23, 1875 in Minneapolis, Minnesota. They were the parents of four children; Lawrence, Alvilda, Ida Marie and Milton
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~
2 CONT
2 CONT per cemetery record: Cause of Death: pneumonia  Age: 72 yr 2 mo 19 days Place of Death: 1304 Stevens Ave So Burial Date: Aug. 27, 1907
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Gift 
2 CONT
2 CONT 23 Des 1875
2 CONT
2 CONT Kilder 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.[S3] Lærdal Bygdebok II, Espe, Alfred - Hovland, Kåre, (Lærdal Kommune, 1990), side 223.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.[S108] Lysnes of Lærdal, a Lysne, (privately printed).
2 CONT
2 CONT [1, 2] 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Lauritz Solberg from Trondheim, was one of the first policemen in Minneapolis.
