1 NAME Elisha Rodolphus /Sprague/
2 GIVN Elisha Rodolphus
2 SURN Sprague
2 _MARNM Sprague
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 14 FEB 1817
2 ADDR
3 CITY Killingly
3 STAE CT
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 22 JUL 1867
2 ADDR
3 CITY Guayaquil
3 STAE Guayas
3 CTRY Ecuador
1 OCCU Lawyer
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Elisha Rodolphus Sprague, son of Elisha L. and Clarissa (Day) Sprague, was born in Killingly, Ct., Feb. 14, 1817; fifted for college at Plainfield Academy, Ct. Principal of Denton Academy, Md., and studying law wit
2 CONC h Hod. James L. Bartol, two yeurs ; admitted to the bar, 184.5: practised in Denton, Md., '43—'45; at Baltimore, Md., '45—'67. Died from yellow fever, at Guayaquil, Ecuador, S. A., July 23, 1867, while there on business. Married. 
2 CONC May 1, 1845, Alida Margaret, dau. of Pierre Cherbonnier, Esq., of New Orleans. La., who died May 4, 1864. Two children.
2 CONT
