1 OCCU Physician
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT HENRY ALLEN WHITMARSH, Providence, Rhode Island, was born there September 29, 1854, son of Edwin Barney and Harriet (Barden) Whitmarsh. He was educated in the public schools of Providence, the Mowry and Goff private school, 1868-1
2 CONC 872, and Brown University, in which he spent four years, 1872-1876, graduating A. B., 1876; A. M., 1880. He studied for the medical profession in Columbia and the New York Homoeopathic Medical Colleges, graduating from the latter 
2 CONC in the class of '79, with the degree of M. D. Immediately after his graduation he entered into practice of his profession. The winter of 1884-1885 was spent in special study in Vienna. He was assistant surgeon to the out-patient d
2 CONC epartment of the Chambers Street Hospital, New York city, in 18871888, and for many years held the position of surgeon to the Rhode Island Homoeopathic Hospital. He has been president of the Massachusetts Surgical and Gynecologica
2 CONC l Society, and the Rhode Island Homoeopathic Medical Society, and is still a member of the latter. also a member of the Massachusetts Homoeopathic Medical and the Massachusetts Surgical and Gynecological societies, the Congregatio
2 CONC nal Club of Rhode Island, and the University Club. Dr. Whitmarsh has been twice married: first with Martha M. Gerst, June 16, 1881. She died May 8, 1888, and on October 2, 1895, he married Alida E. Sprague. Of this marriage there 
2 CONC were born two children, Esther A. and Martha S. Whitmarsh.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://books.google.com/books?pg=PA214&lpg=PA214&dq=Henry+Allen+Whitmarsh+1854&sig=aP3qb30YZ_LRUvviK5W5z0cjEnI&ei=kfzhUMSpFq-UigKS8ICoCg&id=NCkJAAAAIAAJ&ots=tBk-e_6fLk&output=text
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliographic information QR code for History of homeopathy and its institutions in America Title	History of homeopathy and its institutions in America, Volume 4 History of homeopathy and its institutions in America, History of ho
2 CONC meopathy and its institutions in America Editor	William Harvey King Publisher	Lewis Publishing Company, 1905
2 CONT
