2 CONT
2 CONT P. Hansen, Illustreret dansk Litteraturhistorie, 1902
2 CONT
2 CONT Prime Minister of Denmark
2 CONT
2 CONT In office 21 April 1853 – 12 December 1854
2 CONT
2 CONT Born	21 December 1778
2 CONT
2 CONT Died	1 May 1860 (aged 81)
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders Sandøe Ørsted (21 December 1778 – 1 May 1860) was a Danish politician and jurist. He served as the Prime Minister of Denmark in 1853-1854 as leader of the Cabinet of Ørsted.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is considered one of the most important jurists in 19th century Danish legal history. He was a pioneer of connecting jurisprudence and practice and both as a judge and as an author, he successfully worked on making practice the
2 CONC  foundation of legislation. Relatively early, he was connected to the state administration and from 1825 to 1848, he was “generalprokurør” (juridical adviser of the government).
2 CONT
2 CONT His political career was one of paradoxes. As a royal councillor of the absolute monarchy, he was rather liberal and tolerant and therefore often unpopular with the more conservative elements. As the opposition grew stronger howev
2 CONC er, he became more conservative and as prime minister, he was considered a full-blood reactionary. His attempt to charter a very conservative constitution led to cooperation between the king and the liberals that forced him to res
2 CONC ign. In 1855, he was impeached on the charge of breaking the constitution, but he was acquitted and retired to private life.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the brother of the famous physicist Hans Christian Ørsted (1777-1851), and uncle of the botanist Anders Sandøe Ørsted (1816-1872).
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT
2 CONT Dansk Biografisk Leksikon, vol. 16, 1984.
2 CONT
2 CONT Svend Thorsen: De danske ministerier, vol 1., Copenh. 1967.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Anders Sandøe Ørsted (21. december 1778  i Rudkøbing – 1. maj 1860) var en dansk retslærd, embedsmand og minister, bl.a. var han Danmarks 3. statsminister  efter indførelsen af Junigrundloven. Han betragtes også som en af Den dans
2 CONC ke Guldalders hovedpersoner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Faren, Søren Christian Ørsted (1750 - 1822), var apoteker i Rudkøbing, fra 1807 i Sorø, fra 1812 i Roskilde, og blev i 1814 assessor pharmaciæ og forstander for Københavns fattigvæsens medicinaldispensationsanstalt, moren, Karen f
2 CONC ødt Hermansen, døde 1793.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anders_Sand%C3%B8e_%C3%98rsted
