1 NOTE Obituary from The Seattle Times  Feb. 6, 1958 p. 45
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Henry P. Grant
2 CONT      Private funeral services for Mrs. Amy Wood Grant, 76, of Seahurst, a Washington pioneer, were held yesterday in the Bleitz Chapel, followed by cremation.  
2 CONT      Mrs. Grant died in a rest home Tuesday after a long illness.  She was the widow of Henry P. Grant, a pioneer Seattle automobile dealer.
2 CONT      A native of La Crosse, Wis., Mrs Grant went to Port Madison in 1886 with her parents, Franklin and Emmaline Wood.  The family came to Seattle shortly after the fire of 1889.
2 CONT      Mr. and Mrs. Grant were married in 1904.  She was a member of Southgate Chapter No. 190, Order of Eastern Star and the Pioneer Association of Washington.  Mr Grant died---.
2 CONT      Survivors are two daughters, Mrs. Humbert Martin and Mrs. Robert Steiner, both of Seahurst; a son, Vernon H. Grant, Redlands, Calif; a brother, Clarence Wood, San Diego; two sisters, Mrs. Hazel Grant, Seattle, and Mrs. Maude 
2 CONC Bright, Bremerton; seven grandchildren, and two great-grand-children.
2 CONT
2 CONT
