2 CONT Obituary: Seattle Times Tues, Jan. 8, 1983
2 CONT ROSS MCCONNELL, WHO BROADCAST JAPANESE SURRENDER, DIES AT 71
2 CONT    Ross McConnell, 71, who broadcast the formal Japanese surender aboard the battleship Missouri Sept. 2, 1945, died of a heart attack Sunday in his North End home.
2 CONT    McConnell had left his job as news director for KOMO Radio during World War II, and his broadcast of the surrender was beamed throughout the United States by NBC.
2 CONT    In later years, McConnell said he was one of about 300 print journalists and broadcasters on the Missouri, but he got a prize vantage point - "close enough to spit on the table" - after winning an elbowing match with "a pushy R
2 CONC ussian newsman."
2 CONT    It was a high point of McConnell's life, and he re-created that day many times for local service clubs.  The Japanese, he said, arrived in an "oversized rowboat," wearing top hats, morning coats and gray-striped trousers "as if
2 CONC  they were going to a wedding."
2 CONT    There were no handshakes, McConnell recalled.  Among the American "brass were Adms. Chester Nimitz and William "Bull" Halsey, Lt. Gen. Jonathan "Skinny" Wainwright who had surrendered to the Japanese at Corregidor five years ea
2 CONC rlier, and gen. Douglas MacArthur, wearing his "famous cap with all the fruit salad on it" and with his famous corncob pipe, this time unlit, clenched between his teeth.
2 CONT    Born in Bremerton, McConnell majored in English and journalism at the University of Washington.  He swpent 18 years at the Seattle Post -Intelligencer, as a reporter and advertising salesman.  Then he switched to radio broadcas
2 CONC ting.
2 CONT    After the war, McConnell did freelance man-in-the=street interviews for local radio stations, then became district sales-promotion manager for Westinghouse.
2 CONT    McConnell's first wife, Ethel, died four years ago.  He married Blanche Johnson last June.
2 CONT    Besides his wife, he is survived by two daughters, Michele Boyle and Sharon Westin, both of Bellevue, and seven grandchildren.
2 CONT    A rosary will be at 7:30 tonight at Green's Funeral Home, Bellevue.  The funeral will be at 10:30 a.m. tomorrow, also at Green's.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary: Seattle Times Tues Jan. 8, 1983
2 CONT ROSS S. MCCONNELL
2 CONT Of Seattle, Jan. 16, at 71 years.  Husband of Bee.  Father of Mrs. Richard (Sharon) Westin and Mrs. Michael (Michele) Boyle, both Bellevue.  Grandfather of Bradley, Kathleen and Michele Westin, Terrance, Stephen, Laurie and Patric
2 CONC k Boyle.  Christian Wake service Tuesday, 7:30 p.m., funeral service Wednesday 10:30 a.m., both at  
2 CONT GREEN'S BELLEVUE FUNERAL HOME
2 CONT 1215 140th Ave. S.E.
2 CONT Mr. McConnell will lie in state Tuesday, 9 a.m. to 9 p.m.
