2 CONT  E. F. Wheeler obit - 1972 
2 CONT   Author: cathy gowdy  Date: 13 Jun 2001 12:00 PM GMT  
2 CONT   Surnames: WHEELER, CLEAVELAND, ORTMAN 
2 CONT   Classification: Obituary 
2 CONT Post Reply | Mark Unread | Report Abuse   Print Message  
2 CONT Independent Journal
2 CONT Wednesday, July 5, 1972
2 CONT Page 4
2 CONT
2 CONT E. F. WHEELER
2 CONT
2 CONT E. Ford Wheeler of Mill Valley died yesterday in a local hospital after a long illness. He was 83.
2 CONT
2 CONT A native of Plymouth, Wis., he had lived in California 42 years and in Marin County 17 years, residing at 114 Del Casa Drive. Prior to his retirement he was sales manager for Select Foods and had worked in the food industry all hi
2 CONC s adult life.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wheeler is survived by two daughters, Catherine W. Cleaveland and Dorothy W. Ortman, both of Mill Valley, and three grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral will be at 2 p.m. tomorrow at Russell and Gooch Funeral Chapel in Mill Valley. Burial will be private. The family prefers contributions to a favorite charity.
2 CONT ____________
2 CONT A Death Notice in the same paper adds information: he died in Kentfield, and was the husband of the late Olga Gran Wheeler.
