1 NOTE SSDI:
2 CONT Name Birth Date Death Date Last Residence(City,County,State) Issued SSN 
2 CONT Catherine W. Cleaveland 29 Nov 1915 18 Feb 2004 Fair Oaks, Sacramento, California California (Before 1951 ) 548-05-1563
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Obit.
2 CONT Catherine Wheeler (Kay) Cleaveland      
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT CLEAVELAND, Catherine
2 CONT (Kay) Wheeler
2 CONT A 49-year resident of 13 Olive Street, Mill Valley, California, passed away Wednesday, February 18, 2004, in Fair Oaks, California at the age of 88 years. She is survived by her daughter Marilyn Lincoln Pearce and son-in-law James
2 CONC  E. Pearce of Fair Oaks; granddaughters Rosalyn R. Pearce of Sacramento and Catherine L. Pearce of Berkeley; and sister Dorothy Ortman of Santa Rosa. Born November 29, 1915 in Seattle, Washington, she attended UCLA and developed a
2 CONC  career in fashion sales. In 1939 she married John R. Lincoln with whom she had one child, Marilyn Kay Lincoln. In 1950 she moved to Marin and began a long and successful career at the Emporium Department Store on Market Street wh
2 CONC ere she became their bridal buyer, a position she held until her retirement in 1978. She was very close to her sister Dottie and the whole Ortman family. She leaves behind her nephews Norman and Howard Ortman and their families. I
2 CONC n 1971 she married the widower Frederick M. Cleaveland and became step-mother and grandmother to Fred's children: Jim, John and Jane, grandchildren: Ben, Rachel, Geoff and Suzi and great-grandchildren: Rees and Ella Rose, most of 
2 CONC whom live in the Bay Area. Kay loved her extended family and friends, a good golf game, travel, her Episcopal Church of Our Savior associations, playing challenging bridge, sewing designer clothes, following the Giants and 49'er's
2 CONC  and her welcoming home. She was very simply a nice, positive, loving, honest and active person. She lived a long, happy and productive life. She will be missed by all who knew her. The family will hold a private memorial at a lat
2 CONC er date. Donations in her memory may be made to Sacramento Valley Conservancy and mailed to Citizens to Save the Bluffs, 8060 Capitola Ave., Fair Oaks CA 95628. For more information visit the Web site www.savetheb luffs.org or cal
2 CONC l 916-801-7935. 
2 CONT Published in the Sacramento Bee from 2/21/2004 - 2/22/2004.
